From e11a318393dc6c3d6092d2a22d9c30727cce2bbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:56:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(web): encode session list responses in the pool thread,
 not with jsonable_encoder on the loop [daveey]

GET /api/profiles/sessions (Desktop polls it ~0.7/s, limit=200) returned a dict from its
coalesced pool-thread read, so FastAPI's serialize_response -> jsonable_encoder walked the
whole page on the event loop (41 of 185 MainThread py-spy samples on a Mac serve).

New hermes_cli/web_json_response.py:
- native_json_response(payload): JSONResponse(content=payload) built where it is called;
  a payload json.dumps refuses (TypeError/ValueError: datetime, set, Path, dataclass, Enum,
  NaN) is returned unchanged so FastAPI's jsonable_encoder path handles it exactly as before;
  a Response is returned as is.
- encoded_in_thread(func): functools.wraps wrapper running func then native_json_response in
  the same worker thread (signature/annotations unchanged for FastAPI and coalesced_read).
- per_request_response(result): coalesced reads and caches hand one result to several
  requests, but Starlette sends response.raw_headers as the start message's header list
  (CORS appends to it in place) and FastAPI sets response.background, so a JSONResponse
  object must not be sent twice. The rendered body is shared; each request gets its own
  constant-time Response with the same status, content-type and content-length.

Routes changed (same mechanical change, miss and cache-hit paths):
- GET /api/profiles/sessions (coalesced read)
- GET /api/profiles/sessions/sidebar and GET /api/profiles/projects/tree
  (_sidebar_singleflight_cache: coalesced miss + threadpool cache hit)
- GET /api/sessions (coalesced read + SESSION_LIST_CACHE peek hit)
Direct Python callers (get_profiles_sessions, get_profiles_sessions_sidebar, ...) still
return dicts. Left unchanged: /api/profiles/sessions/stamps (sync def endpoint, FastAPI
already runs it in the threadpool but encodes on the loop; not the same change), POST and
mutating routes, and routes with injected Response/response_model/non-200 status.

Proof:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_web_json_response.py (17 tests): RED on parent (4 route tests fail:
  jsonable_encoder ran for a JSON-native payload), GREEN here. Byte equality vs
  JSONResponse(jsonable_encoder(payload)) on 220 fixture rows; 8 non-native payloads take
  the parent path with the same response or error; two coalesced requests through CORS
  each get the full body and single vary/ACAO headers.
- 9/9 spot mutants killed (passthrough, fallback, shared Response, raw miss/hit paths on
  each route, loop-side encode).
- 118 related files: 1413 passed, 19 skipped.
- Bench (hub worker, real profiles router via httpx ASGITransport, 40 requests x 2 rounds):
  200 rows / 115,594 B: loop-thread CPU 8.33 -> 0.69 ms, process CPU 10.2 -> 3.8 ms per request.
  500 rows / 289,945 B: loop-thread CPU 20.0 -> 0.72 ms, process CPU 25.0 -> 8.3 ms.
  Body sha256, content-length and content-type identical before/after.
